# Per-raw landing strategy (10 entries — airgenome-DIRECT only)

## raw 109 — adversarial co-evolution probe
@r109_raw_id raw_109_adversarial_co_evolution_probe
@r109_raw_concept Two systems (defender + attacker) evolve in lockstep; each adapts to the other's current best policy. Defender = airgenome anomaly-detection pipeline (probe→harvest→label→forecast); attacker = adversarial perturbation generator that maximizes label-miss-rate or forecast-MAE while staying within 6-axis vitals envelope.
@r109_airgenome_landing_primary /Users/ghost/core/airgenome/modules/probe.hexa  # already-existing probe module; extend with @co_evolution_loop annotation declaring (a) attacker-update cadence, (b) defender-retrain trigger, (c) adversarial perturbation injection vector for paired-probe mode (probe + adversarial_perturbation = paired sample emit).
@r109_airgenome_landing_secondary /Users/ghost/core/airgenome/modules/label.hexa  # adversarial-rule-mining loop — attacker tries to evade existing 5 rules (rules SSOT in config/label_rules.jsonl); defender mines new counter-rule when miss-rate > threshold.
@r109_minimal_reproducer_pointer modules/probe.hexa header docstring — extend with @co_evolution_loop annotation; modules/label.hexa rule-table loop — extend with @adversarial_miss_rate_ceiling falsifier.
@r109_tracking_id airgenome/convergence/issues/TBD-r109-co-evolution-loop-formalization
@r109_dependencies probe.hexa stable + label.hexa stable + config/label_rules.jsonl SSOT (5 rules canonical).
@r109_witness_cycle_handle 2026-04-XX_r109-airgenome-co-evolution-loop-extension_omega_cycle  (downstream)

## raw 110 — systematic ablation, causal core
@r110_raw_id raw_110_systematic_ablation_causal_core
@r110_raw_concept N-component system → enumerate all 2^N - 1 non-empty subsets, measure detection-coverage on each, isolate component(s) whose removal causes >X% coverage-drop. Causal core = minimal subset of {CPU, RAM, GPU, NPU, Power, IO} axes that preserves ≥(1-ε)·anomaly-detection-rate. N=6 → 2^6 - 1 = 63 ablation configurations (tractable cost).
@r110_airgenome_landing_primary /Users/ghost/core/airgenome/modules/  # NEW candidate file: modules/ablation_causal_core.hexa — orchestrate harvest+label repeatedly with each axis subset, identify causal-core axis subset for each anomaly type.
@r110_airgenome_landing_secondary /Users/ghost/core/airgenome/core/test/core_test.hexa  # extend self-test with --ablate-axis <axis_idx,...> CLI flag enabling subset-measurement loop.
@r110_minimal_reproducer_pointer modules/ablation_causal_core.hexa (NEW) — driver loop over 63 configurations; emit causal-core JSON per anomaly-class to forge/ablation_causal_core.jsonl.
@r110_tracking_id airgenome/convergence/issues/TBD-r110-systematic-ablation-driver
@r110_dependencies harvest.hexa stable + label.hexa stable + 6-axis genome encode/decode round-trip in core.hexa. Cost: 63 × N_samples per ablation cycle — schedule via launchd daily, not real-time.
@r110_witness_cycle_handle 2026-04-XX_r110-airgenome-causal-core-ablation-driver_omega_cycle  (downstream)

## raw 111 — information-theoretic budget
@r111_raw_id raw_111_information_theoretic_budget
@r111_raw_concept Bound any anomaly claim by the underlying channel capacity / Shannon entropy budget. airgenome 60-byte hexagon = 60×8 = 480 bits per genome sample. Total info budget over N samples = 480·N bits. Any anomaly-detection claim asserting >480·N bits of "pattern" is information-theoretically impossible.
@r111_airgenome_landing_primary /Users/ghost/core/airgenome/modules/  # NEW candidate file: modules/info_theoretic_budget.hexa — given genome ring size N, emit Φ_max = 480·N bits ceiling; gate label.hexa rule-firing rate against this bound; gate forecast.hexa entropy estimate against per-axis log2 quantization range.
@r111_airgenome_landing_secondary /Users/ghost/core/airgenome/modules/harvest.hexa  # extend genome-encode path to log Φ_used_bits / Φ_max_bits ratio per sample; >1.0 = overclaim falsifier hit (raw 71 deterministic check).
@r111_minimal_reproducer_pointer core/core.hexa lines 14-16 (GENOME_BYTES=60 constant) — single-source-of-truth for bit budget; modules/info_theoretic_budget.hexa imports via use "../core/core".
@r111_tracking_id airgenome/convergence/issues/TBD-r111-info-theoretic-bound-gate
@r111_dependencies core/core.hexa GENOME_BYTES constant stable; entropy estimator chosen (per-axis Shannon entropy from genome distribution, default candidate).
@r111_witness_cycle_handle 2026-04-XX_r111-airgenome-channel-capacity-bound_omega_cycle  (downstream)

## raw 113 — Bayesian evidence accumulation
@r113_raw_id raw_113_bayesian_evidence_accumulation
@r113_raw_concept Hypothesis H_anomaly scored by P(observation|H_anomaly) / P(observation|H_baseline) updated across N trials. Single-sample rule-fire rejected; cumulative log-odds tracked over time per pid×axis.
@r113_airgenome_landing_primary /Users/ghost/core/airgenome/modules/label.hexa  # currently fires rules per-sample (5-rule SSOT); extend to log_odds_cumulative tracker per (pid, rule_id) — log-odds reset on pid-rotation, accumulated until threshold or evidence-decay (paired with r119).
@r113_airgenome_landing_secondary /Users/ghost/core/airgenome/modules/forecast.hexa  # Holt's smoothing currently treats each genome as point-estimate; extend with Bayesian likelihood-ratio update for forecast confidence interval (level + trend + posterior_variance).
@r113_minimal_reproducer_pointer modules/label.hexa rule-table loop — declare @evidence_log_odds_cumulative as required output for every labeled_anomaly.jsonl entry; emit log_odds_cumulative alongside rule_id + pid + ts.
@r113_tracking_id airgenome/convergence/issues/TBD-r113-bayesian-evidence-accumulator
@r113_dependencies label.hexa stable + config/label_rules.jsonl SSOT + forge/labeled_anomaly.jsonl writable.
@r113_witness_cycle_handle 2026-04-XX_r113-airgenome-cumulative-log-odds_omega_cycle  (downstream)

